# Calendar feeds: RFC 5545 requires CRLF line endings, and scripts/gen-ics.mjs emits CRLF.
# Without this rule, core.autocrlf=true normalizes them to LF when committing from Windows
# while the Linux CI runner (sync-ics.yml) stores CRLF — which churns all three feeds
# whole-file on every sync, and risks an LF-normalized feed reaching subscribers, where
# strict clients (Outlook in particular) can reject it. Keep the bytes exactly as generated.
*.ics -text
